<!DOCTYPE RCC><RCC version="1.0">
    <!-- Runtime paths are :/avatars/NAME - the alias strips the source directory,
         as table.qrc does, so moving the files does not move the URLs.

         THE PORTRAITS A SEAT CAN WEAR. avatars.json is the catalogue: one entry per
         avatar, in the order the catalogue keeps (src/paint/Avatars.h):
         - "id": its name, unique.
         - "gender": "male", "female", or "any" for one either can wear (a star).
         - "strategy" (optional): the bot strategy it is dedicated to. Only a bot
           of that strategy wears it, and that bot wears its strategy's avatars of
           its gender whenever there are any. The names: random, first-card,
           low-risk, ducking, cyborg, reckoner-alpha, reckoner-beta,
           reckoner-gamma, reckoner-delta (newgame::avatarStrategyOf()).
         - "file": the file's name in images/avatars/.
         For example:
           { "id": "cyborg-woman", "gender": "female", "strategy": "cyborg",
             "file": "cyborg-woman.png" }
         TO ADD ONE: put the file in images/avatars/, give it a line here and an
         entry in avatars.json. AvatarTests fails on a file listed in one and not
         the other, and on a strategy the game does not have.

         WHAT A FILE MUST BE:
         - SVG or PNG. Not JPEG: it needs an image plugin the deploy step strips.
           That includes a JPEG saved under a .png name, which loads in a
           development build and shows the bare box in the shipped app;
           AvatarTests checks every .png is a PNG inside.
         - 100 wide by 114 tall in shape, the seat panel's portrait box. Another
           shape is scaled to fill the box and cropped, centred.
         - A PNG at least 400 x 456 pixels; the box is about 140 pixels at its
           largest on screen. An SVG is sharp at any size.
         - Opaque, with its own background. A transparent part shows the dark
           the box is filled with first.
         The client tones every portrait with the mock-up's light sepia as it draws
         it (Theme::avatar()), so a file is drawn as given otherwise.

         The first six are the table mock-up's busts, written by
         tools/export_portraits.py; the rest are the owner's art. -->
    <qresource prefix="/avatars">
        <file alias="avatars.json">images/avatars/avatars.json</file>
        <file alias="man-dark-hair-beard.svg">images/avatars/man-dark-hair-beard.svg</file>
        <file alias="man-hat-mustache.svg">images/avatars/man-hat-mustache.svg</file>
        <file alias="woman-long-brown-hair.svg">images/avatars/woman-long-brown-hair.svg</file>
        <file alias="man-white-hair-hat.svg">images/avatars/man-white-hair-hat.svg</file>
        <file alias="woman-long-red-hair.svg">images/avatars/woman-long-red-hair.svg</file>
        <file alias="man-black-hair-beard.svg">images/avatars/man-black-hair-beard.svg</file>
        <file alias="man-stubble.png">images/avatars/man-stubble.png</file>
        <file alias="man-short-hair.png">images/avatars/man-short-hair.png</file>
        <file alias="woman-long-dark-hair.png">images/avatars/woman-long-dark-hair.png</file>
        <file alias="woman-shoulder-hair.png">images/avatars/woman-shoulder-hair.png</file>
        <file alias="cyborg-man-bald.png">images/avatars/cyborg-man-bald.png</file>
        <file alias="cyborg-man-half.png">images/avatars/cyborg-man-half.png</file>
        <file alias="cyborg-man-eye.png">images/avatars/cyborg-man-eye.png</file>
        <file alias="cyborg-woman-eye.png">images/avatars/cyborg-woman-eye.png</file>
        <file alias="man-black-tee.png">images/avatars/man-black-tee.png</file>
        <file alias="woman-wavy-black-hair.png">images/avatars/woman-wavy-black-hair.png</file>
        <file alias="cyborg-man-gold.png">images/avatars/cyborg-man-gold.png</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
